{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1470568-conceptual-chases","id":1470568,"title":"Conceptual Chases","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-15T17:57:55-08:00","id":1470568,"title":"Conceptual Chases","content":"To confess, I have not used the Chase system very often. As I age, the notion of rolling dice constantly for the sake of the imagination feels increasingly distasteful. Anyway, I'm wondering how often other people use Chases for other, less physical goals, as briefly detailed in every book in which the system appears. And, when you do use them for such, do you still use the more literal chart of modifiers to determine goal numbers (Speed, Initiative, etc)?<br /> <br /> (For context, this is somewhat related to Changeling and I'm trying to gauge a particular mechanic within, but is also universal enough to apply to CoD as a whole.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T18:44:24-08:00","id":1470573,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve been pondering about tinkering the Duel Arcane (Mage) into a modified Chase (right now it\u2019s a modified Social Maneuvering), because the whole Sword &amp; Shield Arcana idea from 1E sounds a lot better as the pursuer vs. quarry dynamic in Chases, but I haven\u2019t hammered down anything clear yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T19:22:54-08:00","id":1470578,"title":"","content":"On the topic of That Changeling Mechanic, gonna link <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1424436-hedge-navigation-examples\">this</a> as much to provide examples as to remind myself to get back to working on that thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T21:49:33-08:00","id":1470583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1470568-conceptual-chases?p=1470578#post1470578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of That Changeling Mechanic, gonna link <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1424436-hedge-navigation-examples\">this</a> as much to provide examples as to remind myself to get back to working on that thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually meant a different Changeling mechanic, but I do appreciate the comprehensiveness with which you approach Hedge navigation; it's helpful to have concrete examples for such an abstract system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T06:25:54-08:00","id":1470618,"title":"","content":"The best Chase system I've saw was one where you break down the chase into Encounters/Scenes instead of just &quot;extended actions&quot;. So a chase through the streets could be broken down into sections of the city it will play through, and each section have a significant event the players will face with a time constraint (they're chasing someone), something to be dealt with with one or two actions/rolls at most.<br /> <br /> You keep tab of successes and failures just enough to know at which scene the chase effectively ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T06:37:32-08:00","id":1470620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1470568-conceptual-chases?p=1470618#post1470618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best Chase system I've saw was one where you break down the chase into Encounters/Scenes instead of just &quot;extended actions&quot;. So a chase through the streets could be broken down into sections of the city it will play through, and each section have a significant event the players will face with a time constraint (they're chasing someone), something to be dealt with with one or two actions/rolls at most.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's exactly like this in <b>Storypath</b> - instead of just 'you need to get 15 successes' - you need in <b>SP</b> to collect Milestones, that are 'this is 1st, 2nd,... part of the project'. Then Chases are naturally split - literal example from my last game session in <b>Scion 2E...</b><br /> <br /> PCs where pursue villain in dark alley - Milestone 1, and they won this 'round'.<br /> PCs running though the crowded street, next to alley - Milestone 2, villain won and 'lost them' - so they needed to look for him.<br /> Final on abandon construction site - Milestone 3, PCs catch the villain with 2:1 result.<br /> <br /> Each Milestone can be mini-scene or obstacle for character to beat them. For ease of use - for each 'you need 5 success' in Complex Actions in <b>CoD</b> mechanics - simply put 1 Milestone as target to achieve. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-17-2021, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T14:04:02-08:00","id":1470658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1470568-conceptual-chases?p=1470618#post1470618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best Chase system I've saw was one where you break down the chase into Encounters/Scenes instead of just &amp;quot;extended actions&amp;quot;. So a chase through the streets could be broken down into sections of the city it will play through, and each section have a significant event the players will face with a time constraint (they're chasing someone), something to be dealt with with one or two actions/rolls at most.<br /> <br /> You keep tab of successes and failures just enough to know at which scene the chase effectively ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules sorta do this already with the changing dice pools IMO; Storypath does seem to make it more explicit though, as wyrdhamster put it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}